_Curriculum_Implementation.pdf","https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Computing","https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/English","https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Geography"],"pageCache":[{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":29506,"contentHash":"865648344d9df7d9214746f99b8888fb8a91bac3f3812df0852936cf1e047cc0","textHash":"66d7ddd18f0bdcdafbd745271f82fbdf2cf2fddeb61e7dedd077e13ae73e6fab","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - Home","section":"homepage","text":"Respecting each other, helping each other and bearing with each other, because getting better never stops.\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay\nWelcome to\nWe are proud of our tradition of providing an excellent, modern Catholic education. At Ursuline College, every student is valued as an individual and supported to achieve their best \u2014 academically, spiritually and socially.\nBeing part of the global Ursuline family, we share a mission to pursue academic excellence, nurture leadership, and form young people of faith and service in the spirit of St Angela Merici. Our values \u2014 aspiration, integrity, resilience, respect and service \u2014 guide everything we do and prepare students to become responsible, active members of society.\nJoin us as we shape the leaders of tomorrow.\nOur Latest News\nOur motto, 'Serviam, I will serve', underpins every aspect of our school.\nOur Trust\nCatholic Life at Ursuline\nHouse Points\nKCSP Trust Information\nUrsuline College is an academy, and part of the Kent Catholic Schools\u2019 Partnership. The Kent Catholic Schools\u2019 Partnership is an exempt charity and a company limited by guarantee registered in England and Wales under company registration number 08176019 at registered address: Barham Court, Teston, Maidstone, Kent, ME18 5BZ. St Edmund's Catholic School is a business name of Kent Catholic Schools\u2019 Partnership.\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA","listItems":["Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay","Our Trust","Catholic Life at Ursuline","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"5","listItemCount":"10"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Modern-Foreign-Languages/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Modern-Foreign-Languages/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":31842,"contentHash":"02f84d1d33f5751a1938cc0917176ad9d82e0388769e46d4331dc74cb5a4da76","textHash":"a6492c4fb53efca363758c6bdb25838794a8617840aabb213592f4c37f4ec681","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - Modern Foreign Languages","section":"general","text":"Modern Foreign Languages\nModern Foreign Languages (MFL) are an important part of our pupil\u2019s education. There are so many clear personal, cultural, social and career benefits in being able to communicate confidently in another language that everyone should have the chance to develop their own modern foreign language skills. We want our pupils to be enthusiastic, engaged, and challenged and to develop their ability to use and understand another language. Our MFL curriculum also aims at encouraging the awareness of our pupils of what lies behind a different language, enhancing the richness and the diversity of different cultures by using authentic resources and making links with pupils from our partner schools in France and Germany. All pupils in the school study French or German and in their lessons, our pupils will gain systematic knowledge of key vocabulary, grammar and phonics of the new language and a better understanding of how these are used by French and German speakers. We want to develop confident and independent pupils who are not afraid to communicate in a different language.\nMFL Department Information and Intent\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3 - Y7\nKey Stage 3 - Y8 and Y9\nKey Stage 4 - French\nKey Stage 4 - German\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3 - French\nY7 - KS3 - German\nY8 - KS3 - French\nY8 - KS3 - German\nY9 - KS3 - French\nY9 - KS3 German\nY10 - KS4 French\nY10 - KS4 - German\nY11 - KS4 - French\nY11 - KS4 - German\nKS3 Attainment Descriptors\nYear 7 - MFL\nYear 8 - MFL\nYear 9 - MFL\nUseful Links/Documents\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["MFL Department Information and Intent","Key Stage 3 - Y7","Key Stage 3 - Y8 and Y9","Key Stage 4 - French","Key Stage 4 - German","Y7 - KS3 - French","Y7 - KS3 - German","Y8 - KS3 - French","Y8 - KS3 - German","Y9 - KS3 - French","Y9 - KS3 German","Y10 - KS4 French","Y10 - KS4 - German","Y11 - KS4 - French","Y11 - KS4 - German","Year 7 - MFL","Year 8 - MFL","Year 9 - MFL","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"6","listItemCount":"26"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/PSHE-Personal-Social-and-Health-Education/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/PSHE-Personal-Social-and-Health-Education/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":30953,"contentHash":"eceb8e5fdf197977f5c0c203da2839ed35d9ddb753b9b2ecdbfda967c56ae256","textHash":"0102c274c7ff8ac4426812acd514dd9127759cc643a7f1ac47c0a491958fadc7","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - PSHE (Personal, Social and Health Education)","section":"general","text":"PSHE (Personal, Social and Health Education)\nThe PSHE curriculum aims to equip students with the knowledge, skills and attributes to be healthy, safe and responsible individuals and citizens. It helps them manage their lives and relationships, make informed decisions, and prepare for life and work in modern Britain. The curriculum focuses on personal development, well-being, relationships and living in the wider world appropriate to each Key Stage.\nPSHE Department Information and Intent\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3/4\nKey Stage 5\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3\nY8 - KS3\nY9 - KS3\nY10 - KS4\nY11 - KS4\nY12 - KS5\nY13 - KS5\nUseful Links\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["PSHE Department Information and Intent","Key Stage 3/4","Key Stage 5","Y7 - KS3","Y8 - KS3","Y9 - KS3","Y10 - KS4","Y11 - KS4","Y12 - KS5","Y13 - KS5","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"5","listItemCount":"18"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Music/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Music/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":30169,"contentHash":"e086363b0ab12645ebf644169d6ae276b1cc90520ad6c474c01f20d83633ab64","textHash":"20b9c2fd4acdf8d131f5ba3abce4bde91174ab52a946c3560e56a1e8fe5529f5","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - Music","section":"enrichment","text":"Music\nFor all of our students to have an appreciation and knowledge of music that they can enjoy for their whole lives, to be aware of the power of music, and have an understanding of the breadth and range of the music that exists, and its place within different cultures and over history. To give Students some basic musical skills that will enable them to play chords on the guitar, ukulele and keyboard, and enough understanding to pursue further musical skills, either at GCSE, A level and beyond, or under their own steam via the internet or books\nMusic Department Information and Intent\nMusic Development Plan\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3\nKey Stage 4\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3\nY8 - KS3\nY9 - KS3\nY10 - KS4\nY11 - KS4\nKS3 Attainment Descriptors\nYear 7\nYear 8\nYear 9\nUseful Links/Documents\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["Music Department Information and Intent","Music Development Plan","Key Stage 3","Key Stage 4","Y7 - KS3","Y8 - KS3","Y9 - KS3","Y10 - KS4","Y11 - KS4","Year 7","Year 8","Year 9","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"6","listItemCount":"20"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Computing/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Computing/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":29723,"contentHash":"baa7e0fd02dd4e9d16566d6a4e73ae2fa8d5b4b39cef180ea9525cb7d07011dd","textHash":"c58aa32342b3e7932ffd37c7af81f3825a36af9660b29934120bf6bac07355dc","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - Computing","section":"general","text":"Computing\nComputing gives students the skills and confidence to thrive in a digital world. At KS3, students explore key computing concepts while also building essential ICT skills that support their learning across all subjects. They develop problem-solving, creativity, and logical thinking through coding, digital design, and practical projects. At KS4, the BTEC Tech Award in Digital Information Technology allows learners to apply these skills to real-world situations, exploring how technology supports modern businesses and everyday life. At KS5, the Cambridge Advanced National in Computing: Application Development helps students take their learning further by designing and developing innovative digital solutions. Across all stages, our aim is to inspire curiosity, creativity, and confidence in using technology to shape the future.\nComputing Department Information and Intent\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3\nKey Stage 4\nKey Stage 5\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3\nY8 - KS3\nY9 - KS3\nY10 - KS4\nY11 - KS4\nY12 - KS5\nY13 - KS5\nKS3 Attainment Descriptors\nYear 7\nYear 8\nYear 9\nUseful Links/Documents\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["Computing Department Information and Intent","Key Stage 3","Key Stage 4","Key Stage 5","Y7 - KS3","Y8 - KS3","Y9 - KS3","Y10 - KS4","Y11 - KS4","Y12 - KS5","Y13 - KS5","Year 7","Year 8","Year 9","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"6","listItemCount":"22"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/English/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/English/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":32013,"contentHash":"ce2aa68fb5c00825489efbbd06a1d30c28e468bf5346864307362865efd45a87","textHash":"de2b967b5c35ec0aeef532f7a2f9fb7eb0b4cc0493e2b30095cb525d7b5c9abf","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - English","section":"general","text":"English\nThe English team strive to share our passion for the subject with all our students. We are dedicated to encouraging the development of individuality, creativity and the love of language and literature. The curriculum is designed to provide experiences for developing thinking and creative skills and to promote a culture of writing and reading for knowledge and pleasure.\nEnglish Department Information and Intent\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3\nKey Stage 4\nKey Stage 5 - A Level\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3\nY8 - KS3\nY9 - KS3\nY10 - KS4\nY11 - KS4\nY12 - A Level\nY13 - A Level\nKS3 Attainment Descriptors\nYear 7 - Reading\nYear 7 - Writing\nYear 8 - Reading\nYear 8 - Writing\nYear 9 - Reading\nYear 9 - Writing\nUseful Link\nAQA GCSE Language Specification:\nAQA GCSE Literature Specification:\nAQA A-Level Literature B:\nUrsuline English YouTube channel:\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["English Department Information and Intent","Key Stage 3","Key Stage 4","Key Stage 5 - A Level","Y7 - KS3","Y8 - KS3","Y9 - KS3","Y10 - KS4","Y11 - KS4","Y12 - A Level","Y13 - A Level","Year 7 - Reading","Year 7 - Writing","Year 8 - Reading","Year 8 - Writing","Year 9 - Reading","Year 9 - Writing","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"6","listItemCount":"25"}},{"url":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Geography/","finalUrl":"https://www.ursuline.kent.sch.uk/Geography/","fetchedAt":"2026-09-13","contentLength":30703,"contentHash":"92e5571d9d7ffdc2cc685f3a68932823481d13b5dff8448e78025af054793d16","textHash":"7d1eea28350f7e9c98b50e3db6328c122b70884a40ab77e439ff1f51b580bd5e","pageTitle":"Ursuline College - Geography","section":"general","text":"Geography\nThe study of Geography at Ursuline College has been designed to develop pupil\u2019s curiosity and fascination about the world and its people; to engage in and enjoy their studies, developing a passion and commitment to learning about our planet and its rich diversity. It aims to expand their world knowledge of places and their locations, investigate places at all scales, from the personal to the global, considering what places are like and how they are changing, recognising that the past helps to explain the present.\nGeographical knowledge, understanding and skills provide the framework and approaches that progress their understanding of the big ideas of geography \u2013 place, space, scale, diversity, interdependence, physical and human processes, sustainability.\nGeography Department Information and Intent\nLearning Journeys\nKey Stage 3\nKey Stage 4\nKey Stage 5 - A Level\nCurriculum Plans\nY7 - KS3\nY8 - KS3\nY9 - KS3\nY10 - KS4\nY11 - KS4\nY12 - A Level\nY13 - A Level\nKS3 Attainment Descriptors\nYear 7\nYear 8\nYear 9\nUseful Links\n\u00a9 \u00b7 Legal Information\nWebsite design by Greenhouse School Websites\nKent Catholic Schools' Partnership\nThe Kent Catholic Schools' Partnership was created in 2012, at the request of the Archdiocese of Southwark, to support and further develop Catholic education in Kent. We currently have 28 schools in the partnership, 23 Primary and 5 Secondary, all of which are part of the Archdiocese of Southwark.\nLatest News\nOUR 6TH FORM\nCATHOLIC LIFE\nPERFORMANCE DATA\nSearch Site\nTranslate Page\nFacebook\nParentPay","listItems":["Geography Department Information and Intent","Key Stage 3","Key Stage 4","Key Stage 5 - A Level","Y7 - KS3","Y8 - KS3","Y9 - KS3","Y10 - KS4","Y11 - KS4","Y12 - A Level","Y13 - A Level","Year 7","Year 8","Year 9","Latest News","OUR 6TH FORM","CATHOLIC LIFE","PERFORMANCE DATA","Search Site","Translate Page","Facebook","ParentPay"],"meta":{"pageType":"substantive","sectionCount":"6","listItemCount":"22"}}]}